  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NIHR Global Health Research Unit on the prevention and management of stillbirths and neonatal deaths in Sub-Saharan Africa  and South Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Liverpool School of Tropical Medicine is the lead institute for the study. Imperial College is involved in WS6, which involves evaluating how best to support parents, families, attending health providers and communities who experience a stillbirth or neonatal death in India and WS5 which focuses on improving immediate new-born care and resuscitation and parent&apos;s involvement in care of sick babies in India.</narrative>
  </description>
